From: andrey-usa <62624421+andrey-usa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:47:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Wide scans with NEON on aarch64

Wide::detect is Some on aarch64, where NEON is baseline, and hits and same compare two 16-byte registers with a one-bit-per-byte mask packed by weight, so the callers are unchanged. The five text parsing copies carry target_feature(neon) on aarch64, and the setup paths take Wide there too. A randomized test checks the masks against a byte at a time for every delimiter value and every offset.
